text:
rachel: heads-up — CI failing on sampleapp publish after typegen run. npm publish gets blocked because package.json version changed during the regen. logs below. :frowning:
ci-bot: [CI] publish-step failed on sampleapp (job: publish:v2) — exit code 1. changed files: package.json, src/types.ts
lee: hmm, did the typegen change ordering again? that usually flips the type hash and then our prepublish script bumps the version when diffs exist. :eyes:
jon: can you paste the tiny diff? I want to confirm it's just property ordering not a real API change
rachel: sure — minimal snippet from the regen diff:
```diff
-  "User": {
-    "properties": {
-      "email": { "type": "string" },
-      "name": { "type": "string" }
-    }
-  }
+  "User": {
+    "properties": {
+      "name": { "type": "string" },
+      "email": { "type": "string" }
+    }
+  }
```
sam: yeah that's just ordering. generator nondeterminism again — we saw this with older openapi inputs. two obvious fixes: (1) canonicalize spec (stable sort) before codegen, or (2) pin the typegen generator to a deterministic build / use a hashless release step.
maria: +1 on canonicalize. also we should avoid automatic semver bumps on publish if the only change is formatting/order. that policy got us a noisy minor bump last week.
lee: quick workaround: commit a canonicalized spec JSON to repo so regen yields same output in CI. longer term: add a `make canonicalize-specs` step before typegen in CI and enforce `git diff --exit-code` to fail early.
jon: do we have a canonicalizer script already? I remember a `tools/spec-normalize` prototype.
rachel: there's a one-off script in infra-tools but not wired into sampleapp. i'll open a tiny PR to run it and commit the canonical spec; will also disable the auto-bump hook for the next publish so we can unblock.
sam: please also add a note to the release checklist — "run spec canonicalizer". :memo:
maria: and we should add a test to the typegen CI job that runs regen and asserts no semantic-only diffs (ordering-only diffs allowed?) maybe do a stable-hash compare of the exported types instead of raw file diff.
lee: +1. for now rachel's approach unblocks. ping me on the PR and i'll review and merge. :thumbsup:
ci-bot: [CI] re-run requested by rachel — publish:v2 queued
rachel: thanks everyone, will follow up with PR link shortly.
